{%- comment -%}
  Usage: {% render 'price', variant: product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}
         {% render 'price', variant: v, compact: true %}

  The compare-at leads and is struck; the price actually being charged follows
  and carries the weight. That order is deliberate — reading "was, now" resolves
  in the direction the shopper is already going, where "now, was" makes them
  double back to find out which number they are paying.

  Restraint is the point. The saving is carried by a struck figure in secondary
  ink and one small pill, not by red, not by a countdown, and not by making the
  live price shout. --danger stays reserved for things that have actually gone
  wrong; a price cut is good news and does not belong in the same colour as a
  failed payment. The pill states the percentage because "Save 28%" is the
  figure a shopper can act on without doing arithmetic, and it is computed from
  the two prices rather than typed by hand, so it cannot drift from them.

  Screen readers get one clean sentence instead of two loose numbers — an <s>
  element is not announced as "struck through" by most of them, so a bare pair
  reads as "1800 1299" with nothing saying which is which.

  compare_at_price is Shopify's own field and is read straight off the variant.
  Where a merchant has not set one — which is every product on this store as
  it stands — the whole block collapses to the single price with no empty
  wrapper, no stray gap and no placeholder.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign on_sale = false
  if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
    assign on_sale = true
    assign saved_pct = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price | times: 100 | divided_by: variant.compare_at_price
  endif
-%}
<span class="price-group{% if compact %} price-group--compact{% endif %}">
  {%- if on_sale -%}
    <s class="price-was" aria-hidden="true">{{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
    <span class="visually-hidden">Was {{ variant.compare_at_price | money }}, now {{ variant.price | money }}, saving {{ saved_pct }} percent</span>
    <span class="price-now" aria-hidden="true">{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
    {%- comment -%}
      Suppressed in compact mode. The card already carries the percentage in the
      badge over its photograph and the cart line has no room for a third
      figure; printing it twice in one card is the clutter this is meant to
      avoid.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless compact -%}
      <span class="price-save" aria-hidden="true">Save {{ saved_pct }}%</span>
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="price-now">{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
